    "source_selection_rationale": "Selected 1,500 training samples per digit from the MNIST training split (mnist_cls_train) for each of the 10 classes. This yields a balanced per-class pool of 1,500 images, totaling 15,000 images across all classes. Rationale for this pool: (1) Domain alignment with handwritten digits (grayscale, 28x28) and image classification task; (2) Consistency within a single dataset family (MNIST) to maximize cross-class compatibility and reduce annotation-conversion issues; (3) Meets the target of ~1,500 images per class across train/validation/test, while staying well under the per-class cap of 10,000 and the overall cap of 50,000 images. The default budget is not limiting here since 15,000 total training images is far below the stated budgets. This pool should support training a lightweight model (e.g., MobileNetV3 Small) that can achieve the target accuracy on CPU with memory and latency constraints described. Note: official validation/test splits will be derived deterministically from this training pool; test/validation data may be used as external benchmarks if needed.",
